  "descriptionKey": "- Coastal bathing water sites are areas of water by the sea or ocean that are used by the public for bathing.\n- Excellent water quality means that contamination levels of E. coli and intestinal enterococci are below a strict threshold. The thresholds are as follows:\n- Escherichia coli (E. coli): The E. coli count must not exceed 250 cfu (colony-forming units) per 100 ml of water in more than 95% of the samples taken over a period of four bathing seasons. This means that in at least 95% of the samples, the E. coli levels must be below this threshold.\n- Intestinal enterococci: The count for intestinal enterococci must not exceed 100 cfu per 100 ml of water in more than 95% of the samples taken over a period of four bathing seasons.",
